    "title": "'Peach Boy' Statue to Return to Guadalupe Park in San Jose - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By San Jose Inside ,\n6 hours ago Plans are underway to replace the cherished Momotaro “Peach Boy” statue, a beloved bronze landmark in San Jose's Guadalupe River Park that was stolen in September 2025. City officials said they are coordinating with the mayor of Okayama, Japan, and a foundry has been identified to recreate the 5-foot bronze statue, featuring Japanese folklore hero Momotaro (the “Peach Boy”), a dog, a monkey and a pheasant. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
